  "worked_solution": "Notice that ${T}^{-1}(D)$ is the image of $D$ under the action of the transformation ${T}^{-1}.$ \n\nLet's find the image of ${T}^{-1}(D)$ in the $uv$-plane. To do that, we write the region $D$ in terms of $u$ and $v,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{-1}(D) & ={(u,v)\\,:\\,1\\le x+y\\le 2,\\,1\\le x-y\\le 3} \\\\  & ={(u,v)\\,:\\,1\\le x+y\\le 2,\\,1+1\\le x-y+1\\le 3+1} \\\\  & ={(u,v)\\,:\\,1\\le u\\le 2,\\,2\\le v\\le 4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
